// States a country can proclaim itself, beyond the regional unions in 00_unions.json.
//
// Every one of these either existed, was formally proposed by the governments involved, or
// follows from something that is on the table today. None of them grants an inch of ground:
// what a proclamation does is put a name, a flag and a colour on a country that has ALREADY
// taken or agreed the territory, and give it the administrative dividend of being one state
// instead of several.
//
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Writing one
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//
//   eligible_tags        who may proclaim it - usually the plausible core
//   required_tags        whose authored territory must be held AND controlled
//   required_provinces   individual provinces, for the cases a tag cannot express
//   minimum_stability    how settled the founder has to be
//   required_ideology    what it must believe, if the state only makes sense that way
//   required_government  and how it must be arranged
//   colour               what it paints on the political map
//   gdp_cost_share       what proclaiming costs, as a share of the founder's output
//   governance_gain      the administrative dividend, bounded by the stability model
//   productivity_gain    and the economic one
//
// The flag needs no line here. FlagCatalog reads what a country has proclaimed as a
// qualifier, so `gfx/flags/flag_formable_yugoslavia.png` is the whole of declaring one - and
// `flag_formable_yugoslavia_communism.png` for the version with a star on it.
